<!--
  Declared breaks against 1.0.0-beta.1, permitted by the repository's prerelease-stability policy and
  required by it to be declared. Three changes account for every entry here:

  1. The framework's stock risk formula is removed so that a Standing Order written to the documented
     contract can actually auto-approve: what counts as risk is the host's to say, and the framework
     owns only the comparison.
  2. A Standing Order and a Referral rule return a verdict rather than a bare requirement, so an order
     held back by one of the three checks degrades to reviewer confirmation on the record instead of
     vanishing, and so a policy can name this write's review window.
  3. Both regain the conversation identity the specification declares an approval policy is given —
     supplied so a policy can BIND (a member-bound Standing Order), never so it can authorize the
     actor, which the framework does itself.

  See CHANGELOG.md's upgrade notes.
-->
